QuestGuidance.Register("en",221,{
[7041]="70065D0B\n1\tTalk to Nestinanessornë\tNestinanessornë lies upon the stone table in Leafshade's grove.\n2\tListen to the conversation of Leafshade and Nestinanessornë\tLeafshade and Nestinanessornë discuss what befell the Elf, and how he came to be in the Ent's care.\n3\tTalk to Leafshade\tLeafshade remembers his conversations with Nestinanessornë.\n4\tListen to the conversation of Leafshade and Nestinanessornë\tLeafshade and Nestinanessornë discuss what befell the Elf, and how he came to be in the Ent's care.\n5\tTalk to Nestinanessornë\tNestinanessornë has collapsed in Leafshade's grove, seeking to go to the aid of his friends.\n6\tListen to the conversation of Leafshade and Nestinanessornë\tLeafshade and Nestinanessornë discuss the Elf's need to leave the Ent's grove.\n7\tTalk to Nakási Wave-reaper\tNakási Wave-reaper and her Corsairs have come to Leafshade's grove.\n8\tObserve the confrontation between Nakási Wave-reaper and Leafshade\tNakási Wave-reaper poses a threat to Leafshade and to Nestinanessornë.\n9\tTalk to Leafshade\tLeafshade is ready to conclude his tale.\n",
[7042]="700147F0\n1\tDefeat Moria Orc-berserkers (total: 5)\030Defeat Dhugluk\tUpon entering Azanarukâr, you are confronted with the battallions of Mazog's elite troops. The Elves have asked you to remove the threat of Mazog in Azanarukâr by defeating their leaders.\n2\tTalk to Magor, the Elven prisoner\tYou have defeated the leaders of the Moria Orcs that Mazog sent to Azanarukâr and found Magor, the lost Elf. Now, Magor wants you to help him defeat the Nameless creatures that dwell deep in Azanarukâr. He will need assistance in putting an end to the scourge.\n3\tDefeat The Gloom-walker\030Defeat The Flame-drinker\tMagor has helped you clear the way to a darker deeper lair. Sensing great danger, he has gone for help, leaving you to seek out the new threat. Seek out the evil ahead and defeat it.\n4\tDefeat Gwathnor\tYou have killed two great Regmyl that have claimed to guard Azanarukâr for a long time. You hear horrible bellowing roars ahead and can only guess at what danger lurks behind the next turn.\n",
[7043]="70061C31\n1\tTalk to Halbarad and hear his tale\tHalbarad weaves a tale of dread.\n2\tHear Halbarad's tale\tHalbarad weaves a tale of dread.\n",
[7044]="700303D1\n1\tTalk to Éomer in Edoras\tÉomer is standing on the approach to Meduseld, the Golden Hall, and wishes to speak with you.\n2\tTalk to Háma\tHáma, the door-ward of Théoden, is before the gates of Meduseld and needs to approve your entrance before you can see the King.\n3\tTalk to Horn in front of Meduseld\030Talk to Corudan in front of Meduseld\030Talk to Éomer in front of Meduseld\tYour companions are outside Meduseld and have been asked to leave their weapons with Háma.\n4\tTalk to Háma in front of Meduseld\tHáma is before the gates of Meduseld, waiting to take your weapons.\n5\tTalk to Háma inside Meduseld\tYou have come into Meduseld with Háma, seeking an audience with Théoden.\n6\tWait for your audience with Théoden\tIt is not yet time for your audience with Théoden. You will be called before him when he is ready for you.\n7\tTalk to Éomer in Meduseld\tÉomer is ready to confront Théoden and his advisor Gríma Wormtongue.\n8\tListen as Éomer speaks with Théoden\tYou have come before the seat of Théoden, King of Rohan.\n9\tTalk to Gríma\tGríma has called you forth to speak to him.\n10\tWitness the will of Théoden\tYou stand before the seat of Théoden, King of Rohan, but it is his advisor Gríma that will decide your fate.\n",
[7045]="7004E17C\n1\tTalk to Dinodas among the misty trees\tYou have come with Dinodas Boffin into the misty woods that border Wistmead in search of the spirit that troubles the Shire.\n2\tCheck the front of the farmhouse\030Check behind the farmhouse\030Check the west side of the farmhouse\030Check the east side of the farmhouse\tYou and Dinodas have found a dilapidated farmhouse in the middle of the misty forest. Can these be the Eerie Acres of which the specter spoke?\n3\tTalk to Dinodas by the cellar door\tDinodas is looking at the cellar door on the west side of the farmhouse.\n4\tOpen the door on the west side of the farmhouse and enter the cellar\tThe door on the west side of the farmhouse is unlocked and will take you and Dinodas into the cellar beneath the farmhouse.\n5\tYou have come with Dinodas to the haunted farmhouse at Eerie Acres, and the two of you should make your way through the cellar to uncover its secrets.\t\n6\tMake your way into the main room of the farmhouse\tYou have finally arrived at the main room of the haunted farmhouse.\n7\tHelp Dinodas withstand the fear that threatens to overpower him\tYou have come to the main room of the old Cleary farmhouse with Dinodas Boffin, and must not give in to the fear that threatens to overwhelm the young hobbit.\n8\tTalk to Bingo in the haunted farmhouse\tBingo and his cousins have come to the main room of the old Cleary farmhouse, willing to stand with you against the Skulking Ire!\n9\tStand with Bingo as he confronts the mysterious spirit\tBingo and his cousins have come to the main room of the old Cleary farmhouse, willing to stand with you against the mysterious spirit... but will it be enough to oppose the fiend's malice?\n10\tBingo has given you the only weapons that might harm the Skulking Ire: the letters Ivy Redsmith wrote to Halson Cleary so long ago.\t\n11\tConfront the Skulking Ire with Bingo and the other Boffins\tThe Skulking Ire rages within the old Cleary farmhouse.\n12\tTalk to Bingo inside the old Cleary farmhouse\tBingo is within the old Cleary farmhouse.\n13\tTalk to Dinodas inside the old Cleary farmhouse\tDinodas is within the old Cleary farmhouse.\n",
[7046]="7005491B\n1\tTalk to Faeron\tYou have entered the Halls of Black Lore. You should speak to Faeron.\n2\tFollow Faeron\tYou should follow Faeron and keep to the shadows.\n3\tListen to the conversation\tLhaereth has entered and is speaking to one who can only be the keeper of the Halls of Black Lore. You should listen to their conversation.\n4\tEscape the Halls\tSomeone, or something, has created a diversion for you! You should escape the Halls of Black Lore!\n",
[7047]="7005A2EC\n1\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hersegg.\n2\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hersegg.\n3\tFollow along with Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.\n4\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hersegg.\n5\tFollow along with Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.\n6\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hersegg.\n7\tFollow along with Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.\n8\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hersegg.\n9\tFollow along with Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.\n10\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hersegg.\n11\tFollow along with Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.\n12\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hersegg.\n13\tFollow along with Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.\n14\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hersegg.\n15\tFollow along with Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.\n16\tLearn the fate of Thrór and the name of his murderer\tHersegg has asked you to learn the fate of Thrór. You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.\n17\tFollow along with Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should listen to Hersegg as she recounts Nár's tale.\n18\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Azanulbizar. You should talk to Hersegg.\n",
[7048]="70034287\n1\tTalk to Horn in Byre Tor\tYou have come with Horn, Corudan, and Nona to the city of Byre Tor.\n2\tTalk to Horn in Byre Tor\tYou have come with Horn to the eastern gate of Byre Tor, and the cold winds begin to rise.\n3\tStay close to Horn and survive your encounter with Núrzum\tNúrzum has returned to Byre Tor! Stay close to Horn, and out of the sight of the giant!\n4\tTalk to Horn in Byre Tor\tHorn is hiding behind a barricade in Byre Tor, as Núrzum encroaches upon his position.\n5\tStay close to Horn and survive your encounter with Núrzum\tStay close to Horn! Núrzum is moving through the streets of Byre Tor and you must not lose track of your companion!\n6\tTalk to Horn in Byre Tor\tHorn has retreated to the stables of Byre Tor, while Núrzum continues his destructive march through the city.\n7\tTalk to Corudan in Byre Tor\tYou and Horn have found Corudan in Byre Tor, but the Elf and the Dunlending were separated by attacking Orcs and now Nona is missing.\n8\tStay close to Horn and survive your encounter with Núrzum\tCorudan became separated from Nona when Orcs attacked, and now she is by herself somewhere in Byre Tor, with Núrzum stalking through the streets.\n9\tTalk to Horn in Byre Tor\tHorn is by the side of a building in Byre Tor. He is desperate to think of some way to keep Núrzum from finding Nona.\n10\tTalk to Horn in Byre Tor\tHorn is by the stables in Byre Tor, trying to come up with a way to keep Núrzum from finding Nona.\n11\tStay close to Horn and survive your encounter with Núrzum\tNona is in danger, but you can do nothing without putting the rest of you at risk! You must stay close to Horn and Corudan!\n12\tReassure Horn that all will be well\tYou have escaped the centre of Byre Tor, but Nona is still in danger! Horn is at a loss, and does not know what he can do to help her.\n13\tTalk to Nona in Byre Tor\tNona has given Núrzum the slip, much to your relief and that of your companions... especially Horn.\n",
[7049]="70035C32\n1\tLeave Drû Vádokan and travel to the forest's edge\tThe forest's edge can be found outside the eastern gate of Drû Vádokan in north-western Balewood. You are standing inside Drû Vádokan, the White Hand's base in the Balewood. You must travel to the forest's edge and wreak havoc upon the Men of Wildermore.\n2\tJourney into Wildermore and defeat any that stand in your way\tThe forest's edge lies to the south-east in Whitshaws. You have found yourself beset on all sides by denizens of the forest. You should continue travelling to the east, but be sure to defeat any that stand in your way.\n3\tJourney into Wildermore and defeat any that stand in your way\tThe forest's edge lies to the south-east in Whitshaws. The trees of the Balewood are enraged at your presence in the woods. You must defeat them if you are to seek your revenge on the Men of Wildermore.\n4\tTalk to the strange tree, Duskleaf\tDuskleaf is standing in northern Balewood. You have found your path blocked by a strange tree that is looking at you with a mix of anger and confusion. You should speak with this tree before continuing eastward.\n5\tJourney deeper into the forest\tThe lands of Men lay to the east beyond the forest's edge. You have defeated the Ent, Duskleaf. You should now continue eastward and fulfil the bargain that you made with Saruman.\n",
[7050]="70009E66\n1\tTalk to Sara Oakheart\tFollow Sara Oakheart into the heart of Barad Gúlaran.\n2\tFollow Sara Oakheart deeper into Barad Gúlaran\tFollow Sara Oakheart into the heart of Barad Gúlaran.\n",
[7051]="70028FAA\n1\tDiscover the source of the Dunlending supplies\tDiscover the source of the Dunlending supplies.\n2\tFind the first store of supplies\030Destroy the first store of supplies\tSeek out the first store of supplies.\n3\tSearch across the bridge for supplies\030Destroy the second store of supplies\tSeek out the second store of supplies.\n4\tFind the third store of supplies\030Destroy the third store of supplies\tSeek out the third store of supplies.\n5\tReturn to the entrance of the cavern\tHead to the cave entrance to make your escape.\n",
[7052]="7002A7E5\n1\tTalk to Quickbeam\tSpeak with Quickbeam.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam\tSpeak with Quickbeam\n",
[7053]="7004DAD0\n1\tTalk to Tárasánë, the Green Lady\tTárasánë is in the Pristine Glade. You and Tárasánë appear to be in the Pristine Glade. You should speak to her and learn how this has come to be.\n2\tVisions of the Green Lady can be found within your dream of the Pristine Glade. The Green Lady has asked you to seek out the visions that have crept into your dream of the Pristine Glade.\t\n3\tTalk to Tárasánë, the Green Lady\tTárasánë is in the Pristine Glade. Tárasánë stands before the Great Tree of the Pristine Glade. You have witnessed the three visions she bestowed upon you, and you should now speak to her once more.\n",
[7054]="7002BFC1\n1\tTalk to Haldir within Lothlórien\tHaldir is in the woods of Lothlórien.\n2\tTalk to Haldir within Lothlórien\tHaldir is in the woods of Lothlórien, waiting to speak with you.\n3\tTalk to Nona in Galadriel's garden\tNona is in the gardens of Galadriel, and wants to speak with you.\n4\tTalk to Galadriel and describe to her your dream\tGaladriel is waiting to speak with you in her gardens.\n5\tTalk to Gandalf\tAgainst all your hopes, Gandalf has returned!\n6\tTalk once more to Gandalf\tGandalf is in Galadriel's garden, waiting to speak with you.\n7\tTalk to Galadriel\tGaladriel is in her garden, waiting to speak with you.\n",
[7055]="7003178C\n1\tTalk to Winsig\tWinsig is standing outside the east gate of Snowbourn. Winsig has ridden with you to Snowbourn in hopes of fending off an Orc assault on the town. It seems you are already too late!\n2\tDefend Winsig as she enters Snowbourn\tWinsig has gone to find Fastred. You should aid the people of Snowbourn in repelling the Orc assault.\n3\tFind and talk to Gísling\tGísling can be found in south-eastern Snowbourn. Winsig asks that you find and aid Gísling and the people of Snowbourn while she seeks out Fastred.\n4\tDefend Gísling\tGísling can be found in eastern Snowbourn. He is overwhelmed defending the city from the siege and requires your aid.\n5\tFight your way to the north gate of Snowbourn\tGísil is said to be near the north gate of Snowbourn. Gísling has moved to aid the people of Snowbourn and asks that you seek the aid of his father and Fastred.\n6\tTalk to Gísil\tGísil is standing at the north gate of Snowbourn. Gísil and his men were struck by a vicious assult of Orcs. Gísil is wounded, but seeks to locate Fastred.\n7\tFight your way to the Mead Hall of Snowbourn\tGísil is in northern Snowbourn, and has asked you to follow him to the Mead Hall in hopes of meeting with Fastred.\n8\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred is standing outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. Fastred has emerged from the Mead Hall. You should speak to him at once.\n9\tConfront Crúmgam\tAs the sky darkens, a familiar figure appears in Snowbourn. You should confront this man, and put and end to his villainy.\n10\tDefeat Crúmgam's forces\tFastred now seeks to exact his revenge on his son's abductor.\n11\tDefeat Crúmgam\tCrúmgam stands outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. Fastred's vigour is renewed after the safety of his son was assured. Crúmgam must be defeated to return peace to Snowbourn.\n12\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred is standing in central Snowbourn. Crúmgam has been defeated and the Orc force is broken. Fastred, his Thanes, and his people are safe for the moment.\n",
[7056]="700451B5\n1\tYou have found Horn in the midst of battle, but the bloodshed is taking its toll on him.\t\n2\tYou have fought alongside Horn, but the horrors of battle are taxing his courage.\t\n3\tStand against the forces of evil\tYou have become held by a powerful and evil force, unable to move!\n4\tDefeat Crúmgam and his allies\tCrúmgam must pay for his crimes against the Free Peoples of Middle-earth.\n5\tTalk to Calenglad\tCrúmgam has been defeated, but not without sacrifice.\n6\tStand with Aragorn as he confronts Gothmog\tYou have found Aragorn and the Grey Company on the battlefield as they prepare to confront Gothmog.\n7\tTalk to Aragorn\tGothmog has fled the battlefield, leaving Aragorn and the Grey Company to mourn the slain he leaves behind.\n",
[7057]="700169DF\n1\tTalk to Narmeleth\tJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith and Mordrambor.\n2\tFollow Narmeleth\tJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith and Mordrambor.\n3\tTalk to Narmeleth\tJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith and Mordrambor.\n4\tDefeat Mordrambor\tJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith and Mordrambor.\n5\tTalk to Narmeleth\tJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith and Mordrambor.\n6\tTalk to Narmeleth when you have readied yourself\tJourney with Narmeleth to defeat Mordirith.\n7\tSpeak to Narmeleth\tSpeak to Narmeleth. With the last of her strength, Narmeleth drove the broken blade into the chest of Mordirith. His crumpled form lies near the collapsed form of Narmeleth.\n",
[7058]="70052797\n1\tTalk to Gultháva, the Maiden of the Gladden\tThe Maiden of the Gladden is inside Kidzul-kâlah.\n2\tMake your way through the torrential passage to the chamber where Gultháva keeps her friend\tGultháva has released the enchantment that sealed the chamber in which her friend resides, deep within Kidzul-kâlah.\n3\tClimb one of the paths up to the centre of the grotto\tSmooth paths of crushed stones climb to a rocky platform in the centre of the odd chamber.\n4\tTalk to Gultháva's friend\tIn appearance, Gultháva's friend puts you in mind of Vágari the Wanderer, but whereas that shade filled you with a sense of dread, this one does not.\n5\tHurry back down the torrential passage and find Gultháva\tA piercing scream shattered the stillness! Has something happened to Gultháva?\n6\tTalk to Elrond in the torrential passage\tGandalf the Wizard and the Elf-lords Elrond and Glorfindel have come to the flooded passages of Kidzul-kâlah.\n7\tLead Gandalf and the Elves to Gultháva's friend\tGandalf, Elrond, and Glorfindel have entered Kidzul-kâlah and wants you to lead them to Gultháva's friend.\n8\tTalk to the shade of Isildur in Gultháva's secret grotto\tGultháva's friend has been revealed to be the shade of Isildur, long kept imprisoned in a secret grotto behind Kidzul-kâlah.\n9\tRemain alert in the secret grotto\tGultháva's friend has been revealed to be the shade of Isildur, long kept imprisoned in a secret grotto behind Kidzul-kâlah.\n10\tTalk to Gultháva in her secret grotto\tGultháva mourns the disappearance of her friend, the shade she held captive for so long.\n",
[7059]="70000144\n1\tGo to the entrance of the Great Barrow, Othrongroth\tThe entrance to Othrongroth is nearby to the west. Tom Bombadil led you safely to the entrance of Othrongroth, the Great Barrow, in the Barrow-downs. Your search for the Witch-king will lead you into the barrow.\n2\tFollow the Witch-king\tThe Witch-king and the dwarf Skorgrím have entered Othrongroth. You should follow them into the barrow and search for them there.\n3\tPursue the Witch-king\tYour path through the Great Barrow led you to the Black Rider, who took notice of your presence and called the Dead to attack you. Defeat these creatures and continue on through Othrongroth!\n4\tSpeak to the Wight-lord\tYour pursuit of the Witch-king has led you to a room with a wight seated upon a great throne. The creature bid you welcome and said that if you sought an audience, you could approach.\n5\tTalk to Tom Bombadil\tThanks to the arrival of Tom Bombadil, the Wight-lord has been defeated! Tom waits to speak with you.\n",
[7060]="7006ED80\n1\tRace westward along the road to Umbar Baharbêl\tRace to Umbar Baharbêl before it is too late!\n2\tRace westward along the road to Umbar Baharbêl\tRace to Umbar Baharbêl before it is too late!\n3\tWarn Khashig of the approaching danger\tKhashig has called for you to stop and explain your haste.\n",
[7061]="70052755\n1\tTalk to Gandalf in the Halls of Memory\tGandalf stands within the Halls of Memory woven by the words of Vóin the Zhélruka, long ago.\n2\tListen to Gandalf's description of Vóin's account\tGandalf speaks to you of the Halls of Memory, a representation of the contents of the Black Book of Mordor given shape by his words and those of the dwarf Vóin.\n3\tMove through the twisting passage until you reach another of the Halls of Memory\tVóin wrote of a journey he took to a \"cold, hard land,\" where great evil dwelt. Further information about this journey lies ahead, beyond the unformed passage that joins the several Halls of Memory.\n4\tTalk to Gandalf in Mordor, as depicted by the Halls of Memory\tGandalf has found the place he sought in the Black Book, and is ready to speak to you of Vóin's journey in Mordor.\n5\tListen to the musings of Gandalf\tGandalf is speaking to you of Vóin's journey in Mordor, where he apparently obtained the Black Book, but the Wizard remains confused about a number of obscured events in the Zhélruka's account.\n6\tConsider the obscured figures in Mordor, as depicted by the Halls of Memory\tSomething befell Vóin among the rocky crags of Mordor, but his account remains vague, the details obscured. Gandalf has asked you to consider the cryptic figures he has found in Vóin's account of his journey in Mordor.\n7\tReturn to the entrance of the Halls of Memory, there to pursue a different avenue of inquiry\tGandalf informed you, regretfully, that this branch of his study has come to naught. Instead, the Wizard desires for you to return to the entrance of the Halls of Memory, there to follow a different avenue of inquiry.\n8\tTalk to Gandalf in the Halls of Memory\tGandalf waits at the entrance to the Halls of Memory, prepared to follow a different avenue of inquiry.\n9\tMove through the twisting passage until you reach another of the Halls of Memory\tVóin wrote of a journey he took in search of Thafar-gathol in the company of King Thráin I, who led the Longbeards prior to the founding of Erebor beneath the Lonely Mountain. Further information about this journey lies ahead, beyond the unformed passage that joins the several Halls of Memory.\n10\tTalk to Gandalf in the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of Memory\tGandalf has found the place he sought in the Black Book, and is ready to speak to you of Vóin's journey in the Grey Mountains.\n11\tConsider the obscured figures in the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of Memory\tGandalf has told you that despite failing to find Thafar-gathol, Vóin found something of interest in the Grey Mountains, and he has asked you to consider what it might have been.\n12\tListen to Gandalf's thoughts concerning Vóin's encounter with Magoldir\tWhile adventuring in the Grey Mountains, Vóin encountered an Elf named Magoldir, who claimed to oppose evil in all of its forms. According to the Wizard, the name \"Magoldir\" occurs frequently among the pages of the Black Book of Mordor.\n13\tMove through the twisting passage and Gandalf will tell you what he knows of Magoldir\tGandalf has told you that the name Magoldir does not appear only within the pages of the Black Book of Mordor, and he desires to tell you what else he knows of the Elf.\n14\tTalk to Gandalf in Mordor, as depicted by the Halls of Memory\tGandalf has told you that the name Magoldir does not appear only within the pages of the Black Book of Mordor, and he desires to tell you what else he knows of the Elf.\n15\tMany questions remain\tGandalf's study of the Black Book of Mordor has raised as many questions as it has answered.\n",
[7062]="70026E47\n1\tTalk to the Dunlending look-out\tThe Dunlending band you have joined is in the fields of Trum Dreng.\n2\tFollow the look-out\tThe Dunlending band you have joined is in the fields of Trum Dreng.\n3\tQuickly speak with the captive\tThe Dunlending captive wishes to speak with you.\n4\tFree the captive woman from her bonds\tIt seems best to free the captive and attempt to drive off this hostile band of Dunlending outcasts.\n5\tDefeat the band of outcasts\tYou must defeat the band of brigands in order to save the innocent village from being raided.\n6\tTalk to the woman you freed\tThe woman from the Stag-clan wishes to thank you.\n",
[7063]="70041246\n1\tTalk to Mister Frodo in the Dead Marshes\tFrodo has slowed his pace. The Dead Marshes are taking their toll on him.\n2\tTalk to Gollum, and let him know how things stand\tGollum has bounded back to you. Your master is right: the creature has not guided you wrong... yet. You still do not trust him.\n3\tMake your way, carefully, through the swamp (press 'Insert' to toggle your more careful walk)\tGollum has bounded ahead through the swamps, showing you and Frodo the way.\n4\tTalk to Mister Frodo\tFrodo looks very tired. The journey through the swamp is taking its toll.\n5\tContinue the passage of the marshes\tThe journey through the swamp has proven to be very difficult, with no end in sight.\n6\tTalk to Gollum and keep a watchful eye on the wretch\tThe journey through the swamp has proven to be very difficult, with no end in sight.\n7\tStay close to Gollum, and make sure he does not try anything\tYou are sure Gollum will try something at some point during the passage of the marshes. Stay close to him and make sure the wretch has no opportunity to cause trouble!\n8\tTalk to Frodo and make sure he is all right\tFrodo has wandered off by himself! You have to find him!\n9\tSit next to Frodo and stay alert for any dangers while he rests\tFrodo has decided to catch some sleep, and wants you to sit next to him.\n10\tRemain awake and alert, Sam!\tTry and stay awake, Sam!\n11\tFind out what Gollum is up to, the villain!\tYou do not like what you overheard Gollum muttering to himself, if you did not imagine it.\n12\tTalk to Frodo and make sure he is feeling all right\tYou hate to do it, but it is time to wake Frodo and set out once again.\n13\tContinue the passage of the marshes\tYou have to go on, even if the Dead Marshes seem to go on forever.\n14\tHide!\tA terrible shadow approaches from high above the Dead Marshes!\n15\tTalk to Gollum, if he can bring himself to speak\tGollum is terrified, and is in no shape to go on. The frightening encounter with the terrible shadow has shaken him tremendously.\n16\tComfort Frodo and decide what to do\tHow has Frodo fared?\n",
[7064]="700583F1\n1\tTalk to Glóin among the crags of High Sundergrót\tThe climb to High Sundergrót has left Glóin quite exhausted, and he wishes to speak with you before you proceed.\n2\tContinue climbing northward among the crags of High Sundergrót\tGlóin suggested that you continue your northward climb among the crags of High Sundergrót.\n3\tSearch the drift of snow to the north, where a glint of metal has caught your eye\tGlóin suggested that you continue your northward climb among the crags of High Sundergrót.\n4\tWait with your companions while they discuss your find and the history of High Sundergrót\tYour companions have rested from their climb and now look around the snowy heights of High Sundergrót.\n5\tTalk to Durin at High Sundergrót\tPrince Durin has come to High Sundergrót and waits to speak with you.\n6\tContinue north-east and climb the fallen pillar lying over the stairs to reach the upper level of the ruins in High Sundergrót\tDurin has asked you to continue your climb to the upper levels of High Sundergrót, among the ruins to the north-east. A sloping pillar lies across the broken stairs that will help you gain access to the upper levels.\n7\tHill-beasts and bats haunt the upper reaches of the ruins perched atop High Sundergrót. You should clear the path of these dangers to make the way safe for Durin and your companions.\t\n8\tExamine the broken dwarf-blade lying near the overlook on the upper level\tA broken dwarf-blade catches your eye by the overlook on the upper level of the ruins perched atop High Sundergrót.\n9\tListen to the words of Durin by the overlook in High Sundergrót\tDurin and your companions have safely arrived on the upper level of the ruins perched atop High Sundergrót.\n10\tTalk to Durin by the overlook in the ruins atop High Sundergrót\tDurin and your companions have safely arrived on the upper level of the ruins perched atop High Sundergrót.\n11\tAccompany Durin on the northward road to war\tDurin is ready to turn once more for the north, and to war.\n",
[7065]="7004A1CF\n1\tEnter the combat area\tEnter the combat area.\n2\tDefeat the first opponent\tDefeat the first opponent. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat the second opponent\tDefeat the second opponent. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tDefeat the third opponent\tDefeat the third opponent. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[7066]="7001B5D0\n1\tTalk to Braiglinn\tBraiglinn is waiting to speak with you at Imlad Lalaith.\n2\tTalk to Raddir\030Talk to Sigileth\030Talk to Achardor\tBraiglinn has brought you to meet some of the Elves you will be fighting alongside during the Golden Host's journey through Mirkwood: Raddir, Sigileth, and Achardor.\n3\tTalk to Braiglinn\tBraiglinn is waiting to bring you to more of the Elves that make up the Hidden Guard.\n4\tTalk to Cúcheron\030Talk to Issuriel\tBraiglinn has brought you to meet two more of the Elves you will be fighting alongside during the journey to Dol Guldur: Cúcheron and Issuriel.\n5\tTalk to Cairches\tCairches is waiting to transport you across Anduin with the company of Elves charged with delivering Mazog to Dol Guldur.\n6\tTalk to Raddir\tYou have crossed the river with the company of Elves charged with delivering Mazog to Dol Guldur, and Raddir is now waiting to speak with you.\n7\tListen to the discussion of the plan concerning Mazog\tThe Elves and dwarves are discussing the plans concerning Mazog.\n8\tTalk to Bróin\tBróin has asked to speak with you.\n",
[7067]="7000B8E2\n1\tTalk to Muildir\tMuildir is hiding by the entrance of Delossad. Muildir is waiting to speak with you before you investigate the ruins of Delossad.\n2\tDefeat Angmarim at Delossad (total: 6)\tSome Angmarim have returned to the outskirts of Delossad to search the ruins. Muildir has told you of the Angmarim that lurk outside Delossad and wants you to defeat them before you search inside.\n3\tTalk to Muildir\tMuildir is hiding by the entrance of Delossad. You have defeated the Angmarim that returned to Delossad and should now return to Muildir.\n4\tExamine unusual items within Delossad\tThe interior of Delossad, known as Sithad in forgotten days, is dark and gloomy. Its walls have seen great sorrow, and a heavy air hangs over all. You are searching within the dim half-light of Delossad for clues to the mystery of Amarthiel's ring, Narchuil.\n5\tExamine unusual items within Delossad\tThe interior of Delossad, known as Sithad in forgotten days, is dark and gloomy. Its walls have seen great sorrow, and a heavy air hangs over all. You are searching within the dim half-light of Delossad for clues to the mystery of Amarthiel's ring, Narchuil.\n6\tExamine unusual items within Delossad\tThe interior of Delossad, known as Sithad in forgotten days, is dark and gloomy. Its walls have seen great sorrow, and a heavy air hangs over all. You are searching within the dim half-light of Delossad for clues to the mystery of Amarthiel's ring, Narchuil.\n7\tExamine unusual items within Delossad\tThe interior of Delossad, known as Sithad in forgotten days, is dark and gloomy. Its walls have seen great sorrow, and a heavy air hangs over all. You are searching within the dim half-light of Delossad for clues to the mystery of Amarthiel's ring, Narchuil.\n8\tExamine unusual items within Delossad\tThe interior of Delossad, known as Sithad in forgotten days, is dark and gloomy. Its walls have seen great sorrow, and a heavy air hangs over all. You are searching within the dim half-light of Delossad for clues to the mystery of Amarthiel's ring, Narchuil.\n9\tExamine unusual items within Delossad\tThe interior of Delossad, known as Sithad in forgotten days, is dark and gloomy. Its walls have seen great sorrow, and a heavy air hangs over all. You are searching within the dim half-light of Delossad for clues to the mystery of Amarthiel's ring, Narchuil.\n10\tExamine unusual items within Delossad\tThe interior of Delossad, known as Sithad in forgotten days, is dark and gloomy. Its walls have seen great sorrow, and a heavy air hangs over all. You are searching within the dim half-light of Delossad for clues to the mystery of Amarthiel's ring, Narchuil.\n11\tExamine unusual items within Delossad\tThe interior of Delossad, known as Sithad in forgotten days, is dark and gloomy. Its walls have seen great sorrow, and a heavy air hangs over all. You are searching within the dim half-light of Delossad for clues to the mystery of Amarthiel's ring, Narchuil.\n12\tTalk to Muildir\tYou have encountered Mordrambor within the depths of Delossad, and he has locked you within one of the cells where Amarthiel was imprisoned. Muildir has come to your aid and will free you from the cell.\n",
[7068]="7006D138\n1\tSpeak with Raphûz to begin the hunt for Kushlâgur\tRaphûz appears ready to enter the scorpion nest. Speak with him to begin your hunt for Kushlâgur.\n2\tSpeak with Raphûz to continue the hunt for Kushlâgur\030Defeat Kushlâgur\tRaphûz looks nervous but resolved to defeat the scorpion Kushlâgur. You should speak with him before you continue.\n3\tSpeak with Raphûz to see how he is\tYou successfully defeated Kushlâgur. See how Raphûz is doing.\n",
[7069]="70071D71\n1\tEnter Jag Golód without arousing suspicion\tEnter Jag Golód without arousing suspicion from the guards stationed there. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tFind Khónyo Bóro within Jag Golód\tFind Khónyo Bóro watching the camp from on high within Jag Golód.\n3\tDefeat Khónyo Bóro within Jag Golód\tDefeat Khónyo Bóro within Jag Golód.\n4\tSpeak with Khónyo Bóro in Jag Golód\tSpeak with Khónyo Bóro in Jag Golód.\n",
[7070]="70071D73\n1\tSpeak with Mizâdi inside the tent\tSpeak with Mizâdi inside the tent.\n2\tSpeak with Khónyo Bóro inside Mizâdi's tent in Ingar-garâsh\tSpeak with Khónyo Bóro inside Mizâdi's tent in Ingar-garâsh.\n3\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Numûru, and Khónyo Bóro\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Numûru, and Khónyo Bóro.\n4\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Numûru, and Khónyo Bóro\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Numûru, and Khónyo Bóro.\n5\tSpeak with Mizâdi once more inside the tent\tSpeak with Mizâdi once more inside the tent.\n6\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Numûru, and Khónyo Bóro\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Numûru, and Khónyo Bóro.\n7\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Numûru, and Khónyo Bóro\tListen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Numûru, and Khónyo Bóro.\n8\tPick up the bowl of food from the table inside Mizâdi's tent\tGrab the bowl of food from the table inside Mizâdi's tent.\n9\tPlace the bowl of food in front of Khónyo Bóro\tPlace the bowl of food in front of Khónyo Bóro.\n10\tSpeak with Numûru inside Mizâdi's tent\tSpeak with Numûru inside Mizâdi's tent.\n11\tSpeak with Mizâdi inside Mizâdi's tent\tSpeak with Mizâdi inside Mizâdi's tent.\n",
[7071]="7002BFB1\n1\tDefeat the Queen of Queens and her brood\tDefeat all insects at the nest to draw forth the queen.\n",
[7072]="7004327F\n1\tTalk to the Lone Lady\tThe Lone Lady can be found at the Crossings of Erui. You have arrived at the Crossings of Erui and should now try to speak to the Lone Lady.\n2\tDefeat the summoned armoured wights\tThe Lone Lady's armoured wights can be found at the Crossings of Erui. The Lone Lady has summoned wights of the Kin-strife to push you from her waters. You must defeat them!\n3\tListen as Roamingstar confronts the Lone Lady\tRoamingstar is at the Crossings of the Erui. You have defeated the armoured wights and Roamingstar has arrived, filling you with hope. You should listen as she confronts her Sister.\n4\tDefeat the Lone Lady's risen armoured wights\tThe Lone Lady's armoured wights can be found at the Crossings of Erui. The Lone Lady has withdrawn in her anger and has summoned more armoured wights to drive you from the Erui. You must stand fast!\n5\tListen to the Lone Lady\tThe Lone Lady is at the Crossings of Erui. You have defeated many of the Lone Lady's armoured wights and should now listen as she speaks.\n6\tDefeat the Armour of the Usurper\tThe Armour of the Usurper is at the Crossings of Erui. The Lone Lady has taken control of Castamir's long-lost armour and now wields it in her final assault against your and her Sisters. You must defeat the Lone Lady.\n7\tObserve the meeting of the Five Sisters\tThe Five Sisters are gathered at the Crossings of Erui. You have defeated the Lone Lady and broken her madness. You should watch as her Sisters speak to her.\n8\tTalk to the Lone Lady\tThe Lone Lady is at the Crossings of Erui. You have calmed the anger of the Lone Lady and should now speak to her.\n",
})
